**C and $O_2$ balance**: $DIC$ flux was approximately the same as in the steady simulation, but varied around 2000 mmol m\(^{-2}\) y\(^{-1}\), or 20 to 30% seasonally. The Seagrass environment retained the large uptake into the sediment from the steady calibration. $DIC$ concentration was close to the boundary concentration of around 2 mmol L\(^{-1}\). In the seagrass environment, the concentration of $DIC$ above 5 cm was closer to 1 mmol L\(^{-1}\). From 5 to 10 cm there was the biggest range of concentration (Figure 12.25).

